// x-typecheck-patterns-15: `graphix-fuzz check` prints AGREE when nothing
// was compared. check_verdict (graphix-fuzz/src/lib.rs:1442) returns no
// divergence for an Excluded-tier program without comparing values (any
// program naming rand::, sys::time, sys::net, throttle, ...: the usual
// `sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(..))` gate makes every probe Excluded)
// and for a node-walk that disagrees with its own rerun; the `check`
// command (graphix-fuzz/src/main.rs:1059) prints every no-divergence as
// "AGREE — interp and jit, no cache, cold and warm produce the same result".
//
// command: graphix-fuzz check design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-typecheck-patterns-15.gx
//          graphix-fuzz run design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-typecheck-patterns-15.gx
//
// expected: check says what it concluded, e.g. "EXCLUDED: values not
//   compared", and keeps AGREE for programs it compared.
// observed: check prints "AGREE — interp and jit, no cache, cold and warm
//   produce the same result" (exit 0), while run shows a different random
//   value in each of its eight modes.
rand::rand(#start: 0, #end: 1000000000, #clock: null)
